> alter bucket Post { Notes lifoStore }
OK  bucket "Post" now declares: Comments (fifo), Tags (hash), Notes (lifo)
> describe bucket Post
BUCKET app.Post
---
Type:               hash
Entries:            1
Logical size:       345 B (before compression and compaction)
Encrypted:          no (this node's store)
Replication factor: 1 (inherited)
Placement:          whole
Indexes:            (none — declare them when you create the bucket)
Stores:             (elements summed over every document)
  Comments     fifoStore  1 element(s)
  Tags         hashStore  1 element(s)
  Notes        lifoStore  0 element(s)
> alter bucket Post { Email string unique }
Error: alter bucket Post cannot add a unique index (Email): this release declares indexes only when a bucket is created:
         create bucket Post { type: hash, Email string unique }
       to add one to an existing bucket, drop and recreate it; note that dropping deletes its data: 'drop bucket Post'
> alter bucket Post { Comments drop }
Error: removing a store field is not supported in 1.0 (Comments drop): it would destroy every document's elements of it in "Post" with no preview and no undo. alter bucket only adds store fields: alter bucket Post { Tags hashStore }
> alter bucket Nope { Notes lifoStore }
Error: alter bucket Nope: server error (1): bucket not found: bucket "Nope" not found in database "app". Run 'show buckets in app' to list what exists, or 'create bucket Nope in app { type: hash }' to create it
